node_modules/
dist/
rust/server/target/
# Cargo also writes a target dir for the packages that are not the server: the
# WASM client builds into `rust/client/target/`, and a direct `cargo test` on a
# shared crate writes `crates/<name>/target/`. Neither is under `rust/server/`,
# so they need their own lines. `dist/` above has no slash, so it already covers
# `nest/server/dist/`.
crates/*/target/
rust/client/target/
# wasm-pack writes the browser-ready package here (`make build-rust-client`).
rust/client/pkg/
/public/
data/
storage/
.env
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
